# fixedbugs, defect 232, lane b8-ffi, 2026-10-03.
#
# A header the machine lacks, named with U+0378, a code point Unicode has not assigned,
# after `fixedbugs-232-`. clang writes that code point back as `<U+XXXX>` in
# *'...' file not found*, on this Mac and on Linux (panel 188's
# compiler-engineer, stage E).
# The reader of that line matched the group's header whole against clang's
# text, so the build stopped at exit 2 with clang's words. It asks each
# group's header in clang's spelling now, a character as itself or as
# `<U+XXXX>` (`emit/clang_name.hero`), and the message names the header as
# clang printed it, so the code point can be seen.

extern "fixedbugs-232-͸.h"
    function seven() -> i32  #~ ffi_missing_header

function main()
    print(seven())
